 "description": "Use this when you need to list the kernelCAD script-runtime surface: global functions (box, path, selectEdges, helix, etc), Shape methods (fillet, sweep, lower, etc), Sketch methods (extrude, revolve, sweep), PathBuilder methods, EdgeQuery/FaceQuery key sets, and featureKindFaceLabels (which globals accept opts.faceLabels and valid value shapes). Use this to discover what is callable from a .kcad.ts script. Call this BEFORE concluding kernelCAD lacks a capability \u2014 its NURBS freeform surfacing (loft, sweep, boundary-fill, G2 blend) is easy to miss from tool names alone.",
